etween 30 June 2020 and Prospectus date (share split, proceeds from employee share purchase, payment of holdback for Inwave SAS, accrued interest payments, redemption of preference shares etc.). These adjustments relate to capital structure and do not expressly restate historical Adjusted EBITDA in provided excerpts.\n- Prospectus notes that non-IFRS measures may be calculated differently by other companies and therefore may not be comparable.\n\n5) Page/table references (Prospectus excerpts):\n- Rounding note: Prospectus page ~21 in excerpt_0.\n- APM definitions and APM reconciliation: Section 4.2.3 and Section 10.7/10.7.2 and note tables in excerpts: pages (per excerpts) ~18, 55, 78, 22–23, 55–78 in provided excerpt numbering. Specific tables:\n  - Consolidated APM table (In NOK million) — excerpt_2 and excerpt_1: shows Adjusted EBITDA 182.6 / 134.2 / 307.5 etc. (prospectus pages ~78 and ~55 in excerpts).\n  - Segment (In NOK 1,000) table — excerpt_1 and excerpt_4: Adjusted EBITDA by operating segments (page ~55 / ~12).\n  - LTM Adjusted EBITDA reconciliation — excerpt_1 and excerpt_2 (LTM table, page ~78).\n\nB. Annual Report 2020 — extracted Adjusted EBITDA figures and reconciliations\n\n1) Exact Adjusted EBITDA values (Annual Report)\n- Consolidated totals (Annual Report tables labelled "Amounts in NOK 1000"):\n  - Adjusted EBITDA — Year 2020: 390,842 (NOK 1,000) → NOK 390.842 million (some APM table shows 390,841; see inconsistencies note)\n  - Adjusted EBITDA — Year 2019: 307,941 (NOK 1,000) → NOK 307.941 million (some APM table shows 307,549; see inconsistencies note)\n- Adjusted EBITDA per segment (Annual Report consolidated statement note / segment reporting):\n  - Northern Europe: 240,485 (2020) ; 194,266 (2019)\n  - Central Europe: 129,283 ; 101,021\n  - Western Europe: 127,826 ; 83,834\n  - Global Messaging: 27,150 ; 26,603\n  - Group Costs: -133,902 ; -97,783\n  - Total: 390,842 ; 307,941\n\n2) Reconciliation tables / notes showing adjustments and their amounts (Annual Report)\n- APM reconciliation (Annual Report "LINK uses the following APMs" table; labelled with 2020 / 2019):\n  - Operating profit (loss) (EBIT): 22,218 (2020) ; -36,955 (2019)\n  - Add: Depreciation intangible assets (and amortisation): 271,389 ; 247,369\n  - EBITDA: 293,607 ; 210,414\n  - Add: Restructuring costs: 47,400 (2020) ; 69,967 (2019)\n  - Add: Share-based compensation: 34,711 (2020) ; - (2019)\n  - Add: Expenses related to acquisitions: 15,123 ; 27,168\n  - Adjusted EBITDA: 390,841 (2020) ; 307,549 (2019) — note small differences vs segment table totals\n  - Operating revenues (for margin): 3,539,231 ; 2,890,025\n  - Adjusted EBITDA margin: 11.0% (2020) ; 10.6% (2019)\n\n- Reconciliation of adjusted EBITDA to Group profit (loss) before income tax (consolidated note table showing per-segment totals):\n  - Adjusted EBITDA: 390,842 ; 307,941\n  - Non-recurring items*: -97,235 ; -97,527\n  - Depreciation and amortization: -271,389 ; -247,369\n  - Operating profit: 22,218 ; -36,955\n  - Finance income (expense): -427,047 ; -193,901\n  - Total (Profit/loss before tax): -404,829 ; -230,856\n\n- Notes to what constitutes "Non-recurring items":\n  - Non-recurring items include costs related to mergers and acquisitions, personnel costs deemed non-recurring (one-off), restructuring expenses, advisors, licenses, sales and marketing, etc. (note text is consistent with Prospectus wording).\n\n3) Units / currency / rounding notes (Annual Report)\n- Annual Report tables are labelled "Amounts in NOK 1000". Thus entries like "390,842" should be understood as NOK 390,842 thousand (i.e., NOK 390.842 million).\n- The Annual Report also uses plain NOK in some parent-company financial statements; when consolidated segment tables use "NOK 1000" the unit is thousands.\n- Auditor\'s report and notes do not flag rounding issues but small table inconsistencies indicate typical presentation rounding or table-level formatting differences (e.g., 390,841 vs 390,842; 307,549 vs 307,941). The Annual Report\'s APM table and segment table differ slightly — likely due to rounding or classification differences; I flag both numbers where they occur.\n\n4) Restatements / subsequent events notes affecting historical figures (Annual Report)\n- Events after reporting date (note 24) list acquisitions that were initiated or closed in early 2021 (e.g., Tismi B.V. closed 10 March 2021 and MarketingPlatform acquisition initiated but not completed as of the financial statements). These are subsequent events and are disclosed but do not restate 2020 Adjusted EBITDA.\n- The Annual Report contains extensive notes on business combinations and the application of significant judgement to measure fair value of intangible assets and goodwill (see note on Business combinations and impairment testing). The Company discloses the methodology and key assumptions (useful lives, growth, margins, discount rate) and that goodwill tested for impairment was NOK 3,982,843 thousand as of 31 Dec 2020 with no impairment recognized in FY2020. These valuation judgments can affect future EBITDA comparatives if impairment or adjustments occur but no restatement is indicated in the provided excerpts.\n- Auditor\'s report: Key audit matters included impairment of goodwill; auditor concluded management\'s assumptions reasonable. No auditor-initiated restatements to Adjusted EBITDA are shown in the provided excerpts.\n\n5) Page/table references (Annual Report excerpts)\n- Segment reporting and Adjusted EBITDA per segment: Annual Report pages shown in excerpts: ~53–54 (segment tables) and ~54 (Adjusted EBITDA per segment).\n- APM reconciliation (EBIT to Adjusted EBITDA): Annual Report pages ~82 and ~81 (APM section and APM table), and the consolidated reconciliation table ~54.\n- Events after reporting date: note 24 excerpt appears on page ~81 in the Annual Report excerpts.\n- "Notes to the financial statements" index listing note 25 APMs is page ~38 in excerpt.\n\nC. Observations on inconsistencies, rounding and interpretation risks\n- The documents present adjusted EBITDA in different units and table formats: Prospectus uses both "NOK million" narrative tables and "In NOK 1,000" segment tables; Annual Report uses "Amounts in NOK 1000" for consolidated tables. Always check table heading to interpret magnitude.\n- Minor numeric inconsistencies exist between tables in the same document (e.g., Prospectus total Adjusted EBITDA 307.5 million vs segment total 307,548 thousand; Annual Report shows 390,841 in an APM table vs 390,842 in segment totals; 2019 shows 307,549 in one APM table vs 307,941 in segment totals). These differences are small, consistent with rounding, truncation, or slightly different classification between the APM reconciliation table and segment aggregation. The Prospectus explicitly warns about rounding and differences across tables.\n- No explicit accounting restatement of historical Adjusted EBITDA figures (e.g., correction due to error) is shown in the supplied excerpts. There are subsequent events (acquisitions closed after year end) and capital structure adjustments in the Prospectus that affect capitalisation and indebtedness but not the historical Adjusted EBITDA amounts shown in the materials provided.\n\n### 3. Additional context (if relevant):\n- If you need exact numeric parity (e.g., a single authoritative Adjusted EBITDA for 2019 or 2020), use the Annual Report consolidated "Amounts in NOK 1000" tables as the formal audited source (Annual Report is audited; Prospectus APMs are based on same underlying accounts but presented for offering purposes). Auditor\'s report in the Annual Report supports the consolidated financial statements. For audited consolidated Adjusted EBITDA for 2020, the Annual Report APM table shows Adjusted EBITDA = 390,841 (NOK 1,000) (i.e., NOK 390.841 million) — the segment aggregation lists 390,842 (NOK 1,000). Choose one and document the rounding difference if needed.\n- If you will be using these figures for covenant calculations or modelling, ensure consistent unit handling (NOK vs NOK thousand vs NOK million) and decide whether to use the Prospectus LTM Adjusted EBITDA (356.1 NOK million at 30 June 2020) or the Annual Report 2020 Adjusted EBITDA (390.841 / 390.842 NOK million for full year 2020), noting LTM is a trailing 12-month measure to 30 June 2020 while 2020 full year covers 1 Jan–31 Dec 2020.\n- If you want, I can:\n  - Provide a side-by-side table that normalizes all figures to one unit (e.g., NOK million) and reconcile the small discrepancies (showing both values and sources).\n  - Extract the exact clause references (document filename, section headings, and page numbers) in the original PDFs if you supply those files or allow me to fetch them.\n  - Flag any areas where the Prospectus and Annual Report APM definitions differ (they appear consistent in definitions shown).\n\nIf you want the numbers normalized into a single clean table (all in NOK million) with source lines and exact excerpt page references, tell me which unit you prefer (NOK million or NOK 1,000) and I will produce that concise table and include the exact source lines and the note texts for each adjustment.'}], tool_calls=None, raw=None, token_usage=None)Message 7: ASSISTANT
